# CAMEL OVERKILL: DASH-1 "REACTOR WALL". Four readouts on the reactor room wall. Each is two text displays: a caption
# that never changes and a short value. A value never scrolls: a long text that changes every second never shows its
# end in game (the scroll snaps back on every change, reference/TEXT_DISPLAYS.md).
name camel_dash_reactor
box battery
note "DASH-1 REACTOR WALL: HOW IT WORKS" "Every value is about 7 characters at most, so it fits its display and never scrolls. The captions (OUTPUT, CORE, ...) are separate displays that never change.\nout1 OUTPUT: power_value_out + ' kW'.\nout2 CORE: temperature_out / 10, rounded, / 10, + ' C'. out3 is its colour: index = 2 x (t > 60) + (40 > t) picks green (optimal) / blue (cold) / red (hot) from a multiplexer.\nout4 FISSION and out5 TURBINE: what HUMP-1 asks for, rounded, + '%'."
note "WIRING" "in1 <- reactor power_value_out, in2 <- reactor temperature_out\nin3 <- HUMP-1 out1 (fission), in4 <- HUMP-1 out2 (turbine)\nout1, out2, out4, out5 -> value displays (set_text); out3 -> the CORE value display's set_text_color"
c k10 mem Value=10
c ukw mem Value=kW
c a1 concat Separator=" "
w in1 a1.1
w ukw.out a1.2
w a1.out out1
# temperature
c t10 div
c tr round
c tc div
w in2 t10.1
w k10.out t10.2 tc.2
w t10.out tr.in
w tr.out tc.1
c k60 mem Value=60
c k40 mem Value=40
c k2 mem Value=2
c hot greater
c cold greater
c h2 mul
c idx add
w tc.out hot.1 cold.2
w k60.out hot.2
w k40.out cold.1
w hot.out h2.1
w k2.out h2.2
w h2.out idx.1
w cold.out idx.2
c g0 mem Value="120,255,140,255"
c g1 mem Value="120,180,255,255"
c g2 mem Value="255,80,60,255"
c gmux mux
w idx.out gmux.set_input
w g0.out gmux.signal_in0
w g1.out gmux.signal_in1
w g2.out gmux.signal_in2 gmux.signal_in3
w gmux.out out3
c uc mem Value=C
c b1 concat Separator=" "
w tc.out b1.1
w uc.out b1.2
w b1.out out2
# fission / turbine
c fr round
c tu round
c pc mem Value=%
c d1 concat
c d2 concat
w in3 fr.in
w in4 tu.in
w fr.out d1.1
w tu.out d2.1
w pc.out d1.2 d2.2
w d1.out out4
w d2.out out5
